Two fonts is plenty: a distinctive face for headings, a plain workhorse for body text. Contrast in role is what makes a pairing work; two nearly-identical fonts read as a mistake. **Leading** is the space between lines, **tracking** the spacing across a run of text, **kerning** the gap between two specific letters.

